From: Capri NixOS maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm4250-motorola-capri: add Bluetooth BD address

The wcn399x NVM image declares 39:50:12:00:40:02 as its factory-default BD
address, and the controller reports that same address. btqca treats a
controller that still has the NVM default as unprovisioned and sets
HCI_QUIRK_USE_BDADDR_PROPERTY, so the Bluetooth core only configures it when
the board DT supplies local-bd-address. Without the property the controller
stays HCI_UNCONFIGURED, hci0 remains DOWN RAW and can never be brought up.

Assign a stable locally-administered address to the Bluetooth node.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm4250-motorola-capri.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm4250-motorola-capri.dts
@@ -485,6 +485,7 @@
  pinctrl-1 = <&capri_bt_uart_sleep>;
  bluetooth {
   compatible = "qcom,wcn3950-bt";
+  local-bd-address = [ 01 00 00 27 12 02 ];
   max-speed = <3000000>;
   vddio-supply = <&vreg_l9a>;
   vddxo-supply = <&vreg_l16a>;
